{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_quzk5govb4s6ddixhxnmjcmiz7jvl6vdty4ejmkf5u6am6dzh3ba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The whole C library is translated and verified.\n\n## Scope\n`c_src/` is a single-module library: `include/lib.h` (1 line) + `src/lib.c` (174 lines), globbed by CMake into one shared library exporting **12 public symbols**. I enumerated the surface with `nm -D` on the C `.so` first, then translated all of it — no namespace-renaming macros were present, so linker names equal source names.\n\n## Completion gate — symbol diff is empty\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| C exports | 12 |\n| Rust exports | 12 |\n| `diff` | **empty**, including matching `T` binding types |\n\n`add_operation`, `multiply_operation`, `subtract_operation`, `divide_operation`, `modulo_operation`, `is_valid_operation`, `get_operation_priority`, `select_operation`, `get_computation_timestamp`, `allocate_results`, `perform_computation_with_history`, `mathop`.\n\n## Differential testing (built the real C `.so` and `dlopen`'d both)\n- **Driver, 11,922 bytes — byte-identical.** All 256 `char` values through `is_valid_operation`; 225 operand pairs (incl. `INT_MAX`/`INT_MIN`, negatives, div/mod by zero); `select_operation` identity-compared against the exported symbols; `allocate_results` zero-init + negative counts; `perform_computation_with_history` NULL-init path, 10-entry cap, and a full struct-field dump; 16 stateful `mathop` calls.\n- **Fuzz, 538,849 bytes / 20,015 lines — byte-identical.** 4,000 rounds of randomized calls interleaved across the API so the `static` history state co-evolves.\n\n## Fidelity choices worth flagging\n- **libc reuse:** `printf`, `calloc`, and `time` are declared and called, not reimplemented — so stdout buffering/interleaving matches, and `allocate_results` returns a genuinely `free()`-able block.\n- **`.so` name:** CMake derives the project name from `c_src`'s *parent* directory, so the C artifact is `libtranslated_rust.so`. I set `[lib] name` to match exactly rather than leaving the default `libtmp.so` mismatch I initially had.\n- **Bugs preserved, not fixed:** the dead `validation_char` store; `param3 % 5 + 1` going negative for negative inputs (falling through `select_operation`'s `default`); the unchecked `*history` deref after allocation; `int`→`size_t` sign extension in `calloc`. Enums are modelled as `c_int` (verified 24-byte struct, offsets 0/8/16).\n\n**One deviation, by necessity:** `divide_operation(INT_MIN, -1, _)` and `modulo_operation(INT_MIN, -1, _)`. These are signed-overflow *undefined behavior* in C — I confirmed the reference `.so` dies from SIGFPE (exit 136), so there is no defined output to be identical to. Rust returns `INT_MIN`/`0` instead of crashing; matching the trap exactly would need inline `idiv` asm (plain Rust `/` aborts with SIGABRT, a different signal anyway). Every input with defined C behavior matches bit-for-bit. Both functions document this. Say the word if you'd rather I `raise(SIGFPE)` to mirror the crash.\n\n`cargo build --release` compiles clean with zero warnings, and nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":603,"cache_read_input_tokens":44192,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":603,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7be85711-8e37-42ba-973f-2a07eb61c55f","uuid":"9f6cea59-7ed2-4cb5-bebb-79195e27d300","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:33:32.753Z"}
